<title>BRAZIL: Brazil NNE sugar exports 35 pct down in Sept/Feb.</title>
<headline>Brazil NNE sugar exports 35 pct down in Sept/Feb.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shipments of sugar since September from Brazil's key north/northeast ports of Recife and Maceio are running around 35 percent behind last year's levels, according to port authority statistics.</p>
<p>Since the start of September 1996 to the end of February this year just over one million tonnes of sugar have been exported against 1.55 million tonnes in the same period the previous year.</p>
<p>A breakdown of shipments per month follows in tonnes.</p>
<p> RECIFE				 BULK		    BAGGED</p>
<p>			  1996/97    1995/96    1996/97  1995/96</p>
<p> September	     18,090     16,000     5,518	   0</p>
<p> October		 46,000     69,000    26,500    54,488</p>
<p> November		43,000    120,427    76,000    86,249</p>
<p> December		91,505    170,080    88,055    74,059</p>
<p> January		 58,983    148,201    56,740    41,548</p>
<p> February		     0     42,189    26,590    55,197</p>
<p> TOTAL		  257,578    565,897   279,403   311,541</p>
<p>TOTAL September 1996 to February 1997 - 536,981 tonnes</p>
<p>TOTAL September 1995 to February 1996 - 877,438 tonnes</p>
